      "text": "To solve for \\( ab + ac + bc \\) given that \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\) are the roots of the polynomial \\( 3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0 \\), we will use the relationships between the roots and the coefficients of the polynomial as provided by Vieta's formulas.\n\nFirst, Vieta's formulas tell us the following for a cubic polynomial \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0 \\) with roots \\( r_1, r_2, r_3 \\):\n1. \\( r_1 + r_2 + r_3 = -\\frac{b}{a} \\)\n2. \\( r_1r_2 + r_2r_3 + r_3r_1 = \\frac{c}{a} \\)\n3. \\( r_1r_2r_3 = -\\frac{d}{a} \\)\n\nFor the given polynomial \\( 3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0 \\), we identify the coefficients as:\n- \\( a = 3 \\)\n- \\( b = -3 \\)\n- \\( c = 11 \\)\n- \\( d = -8 \\)\n\nUsing Vieta's formulas, we find:\n1. The sum of the roots:\n\\[\na + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a} = -\\frac{-3}{3} = 1\n\\]\n\n2. The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time:\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{11}{3}\n\\]\n\n3. The product of the roots:\n\\[\nabc = -\\frac{d}{a} = -\\frac{-8}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}\n\\]\n\nWe are asked to find \\( ab + ac + bc \\). From the second Vieta's formula, we have:\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{11}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{3}}\n\\]",
